# =============================================================================
# mmonfar. // Semantic M&M Failure Navigation Engine
#
# Threat model for this file: someone points the tool at a real M&M register,
# then commits. Git history is difficult to retract and easy to push, so the
# rule is that NOTHING derived from an input file is ever tracked. Only source
# is tracked, and every artefact is reproducible with one command.
#
# Tracked on purpose: SPECIFICATION.md, README.md, tests/, the marketing copy
# and render script, and app/index.html — see the note in the app section.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Environments ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
.env
.env.*

# ---- Python bytecode / caches ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- Editor / OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*~

# ---- INPUT DATA: never tracked, no exceptions ----
# Not even the synthetic mock. `python data_generator.py` rebuilds it
# deterministically in about a second, so there is no reason for a spreadsheet
# to exist in git history — and a blanket rule is the only rule that survives
# someone dropping a real extract into the folder at 5pm on a Friday.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.csv
*.tsv
~$*
input_mm_data.xlsx
mock_mm_minutes.xlsx

# Registers uploaded through the serve.py workbench. This is the single most
# likely place for real patient data to land on disk.
.uploads/

# ---- DERIVED DATA: contains every case narrative verbatim ----
# data.json and standalone.html both carry the full text of every case. With a
# real register that is patient data, so both are ignored.
#
# app/index.html IS tracked, and stays safe because engine.py never writes to
# it: the payload is injected into app/standalone.html instead, and the tracked
# template keeps an empty payload and fetches data.json at runtime.
app/data.json
app/standalone.html

# CSV exported from the canvas, if it lands in the project folder.
mm_galaxy_export.csv

# ---- Marketing ----
# The whole folder is private: the post copy is unpublished work, and the
# rendered media are multi-megabyte binaries that change wholesale on every
# render, which git handles badly. Everything in here is reproducible with
# `python marketing/generate_promo_viz.py`.
marketing/

# ---- Model + build caches ----
.cache/
models/
*.log